    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner creation limit (reject with 429 once 100+ owners have been created today) following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions:\n\n1. **`ValidateDailyOwnerLimit.java`** \u2014 a read-only validation gate (`Validate<E>` naming) that counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the server's current date and throws `DailyOwnerLimitException` when the count is \u2265 100.\n\n2. **`DailyOwnerLimitException.java`** \u2014 a checked exception (extends `Exception`) so it appears in the `throws` clause.\n\n3. **`DailyOwnerLimitExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 escalation handler responding `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`.\n\n4. **`...DailyOwnerLimitException.yml`** \u2014 escalation wiring under `officefloor/escalation/`.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `dailyLimit` step after `cityCapacity` and before `applyHousehold`, so the limit is checked before any entity is built or persisted (consistent with the other read-only gates).\n\nThe gate runs before the `build`/`save` steps, matching the existing `cityCapacity` pattern. `BuildOwner` defaults a new owner's `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()`, so the 100 owners created today count toward the limit and the 101st is rejected with 429. Both the targeted `AcceptanceTest` and the full test suite pass.",
